+# 11 — Scanner real-map fix and exterior geometry: mandatory specification
+
+## Evidence and core case
+User screenshots: ordinary wall scanner at **grid tile (-11,2)** on Briar points **South** into a real enclosed room; comparator scanner **(-5,2)** is mounted analogously and works. `briarKIAS.yml` was NOT modified. Earlier report: (-11,2) `NoInteriorSeed` / zero cells. Treat this as **algorithmic/coordinate defect until proven otherwise**, not user misplacement. Preserve author-built map, rotation, walls and all other devices. Find actual game-space wall tile, exact Transform.LocalRotation including parent/grid transforms, `Inward()` mapping, `ScannerSeed()`, floor/airtight/space status for four neighbors, door overlap, tile grid index and geometry revision. Compare with (-5,2) on same loaded server. Print a diagnostic record with real values and screenshot + cell overlay. Avoid guessing from sprite orientation or rotating device as quick fix.
+
+In `KiasRoomTopologySystem` source archive, `BindScanners` currently uses `cache.Geometry.ScannerSeed(tile, Inward(transform.LocalRotation))`, then silently skips when `At(seed)` is nonusable. Improve diagnostics: assigned room status, source tile, true facing, neighbor list, blocked edges, floor classification, and reason for rejection; no silent skip. Account for wall-mounted placement geometry, where scanner's visual tile can be offset relative to actual anchored/wall tile; determine precise game `Transform` and sprite offsets. Verify four orientation cardinal cases with distinct fixtures, side-by-side (one rotated 180°), south fixture, and saved Briar (-11,2)/(-5,2) parity. Correct code, not map. No global fallback that scans across wall.
+
+## Exterior advanced scanner contract
+Second screenshot: advanced scanner is on a hull edge and looks **outward into space**; cyan outline indicates an **irregular, finite outside surveillance footprint that follows the projecting boundary of the ship on one side**. The image is a product reference, not precise measured polygon in tile coordinates. Introduce explicit `Exterior`/`OpenSector` mode only when outward orientation and hull-exterior seed are validated. Do not reuse `OpenToSpace` bounded circle; do not flood-fill infinite void or entire exterior of ship. Prefer shape generated from **ship hull geometry + facing + distance budget + obstacles/occlusion**; exterior cells may lie off-grid in map coordinates, so room's grid tile index alone cannot represent them. Pick a defensible deterministic algorithm: derive outer hull/occluder silhouette, determine outward half-plane, use tile/grid coordinates and transform to bounded range, restrict by sight/line-of-sight or shadowing of hull geometry, clip to available map/space. Ensure a cutout/stepped ship outline is reflected in shape and near-hull perimeter coverage, no detection through own hull. Exact user cyan shape need not be pixel-identical; explicitly produce visual overlay for acceptance. Exclude different grids only if intended by modules: exterior threat/spectral detector SHOULD detect eligible approaching exterior entities outside hull on map, not only transform.GridUid==source grid. Ownership/automatic control permissions MUST NOT cross grids.
+
+Clarify scanner modes: InteriorRoom = true closed room; ExteriorSector = outward scanner; UnsealedInterior/OpenToSpace = destroyed/depressurized interior or open deck, NOT automatically same as ExteriorSector. Define mode selection using valid seed, facing, real geometry and exterior facing. Invalid ambiguous seed yields status and no permissive circular fallback. `Range` legacy may be used as **exterior** reach and UI shows labeled distance, but InteriorRoom is always full room. Advanced/basic capability differences remain module-based; do not give exterior threat sensors to a module lacking them.
+
+### Door and wall invariants
+Open/closed door remains semantic border, threshold belongs to adjacent rooms; open-door atmos flow must not merge rooms. On wall deletion, affected geometry invalidated quickly; on repair/door removal recalculate exactly; temporary bad geometry never emits phantom positives; transforms and rotations moving scanner invalidate scanner association. Limit exposure across hull openings by clear rules (breach is still interior unless explicitly reclassified) and tests. Reconciliation of `KiasCrewSystem`, `KiasIntegrationSystem.Reconcile/CanControl`, display + service-tool overlay, scanner module reporting all consume one geometry/index. Interior device control must not become global merely because exterior visibility is broad.
+
+### Essential tests and explicit acceptance
+1. Saved real Briar scanner (-11,2) correct room, nonzero cell count, facing SOUTH; direct comparison with (-5,2), diagnostics values; verify module detection inside/behind partition and door threshold.
+2. Exterior left/right advanced scanner: finite region correctly extends outside hull along step/indentation and respects occlusion, detect eligible physical exterior entity at near, edge, beyond range and behind hull; validate reflected/rotated ships and parent transform.
+3. Transparent/solid walls, mult-tile doors and pressure doors, open doors, radiation and fauna, physical player including critical/dead, entity crosses threshold, breach and topology cache invalidation, >40 grids and scanner ownership, no cap/clip hiding missing cells.
+4. Auto-integrated air alarms, fire alarms, vents, doors and direct integrated devices; no scanner `Range` remaining as interior acceptance check; Direct bindings remain and no privilege bypass.
+5. Export `scanner-map-before-after.json` with scanner IDs/coords/facing/mode, room/revision, interior/boundary/exterior tiles/cells hashes and screenshot preview. No `NoInteriorSeed` at (-11,2); if actual authoritative map invalid, report exact contradictory evidence rather than mutating YAML.
+6. 40-grids geometry wave: measure rebuild CPU/latency/allocs/memory and assert stable no rebuild churn; profile source of past observed rebuild discrepancy (9349 vs 344 calls) with reason categories.
