+# 13 — Final FullGame must be full-fidelity, strict preflight verified
+
+The owner will execute the *long* final testing via root .bat; agent builds/validates now, no long run. Seven native driver pairs are insufficient. Require every listed category to have actual native engine interaction + an on-server observable postcondition. Reject missing/null driver with NOT_READY and nonzero exit. Fixtures may be independent from author ship as needed, must remain game-authentic and must not silently bypass combat or FTL.
+
+## Required event classes (all 40 ships, scheduled deterministic by tick)
+- real fire ignition/oxygen/heat propagation + alarms + KIAS suppression + clear; atmosphere drop, vent/pump, breach/repair, real door/airlock state machine;
+- real armed shooter projectile spawn via gun firing path, flight/impacts/damage, exterior weapon-flash detection/IFF, PDC friendly/hostile interception, radar/occlusion/ammo/reload/jamming; expose incompatibility as fixture/capability result;
+- native FTL jump completion into detection radius of second grid + jump out, nav arrival distinct from FTL, scan/disposition, energy rules;
+- physical ship velocity/rigid-body collision (not direct KIAS collision event), damage, hull alarms and collision speed thresholds;
+- real tracked crew with Mind and KIAS-registered transponder serial where required: critical AND dead distinct MobState transitions, revive where native, departure/return, visitors/intruders, held gun/threat, fauna and radiation; count registered/unregistered correctly;
+- real DATA cable cut/restore, topology invalidation, core or rack power loss/recovery, changing doors and structural geometry, simultaneous scanner rebuild, cards and queues persistence;
+- native anomaly progression/clear, radiation, structural damage, lamps and runtime ALL/ANY device fanout.
+
+**Synchronous crash waves:** 40 ships hit exact same target tick (record dispatch tick and real physical state changes): 40 critical, 40 deaths, 40 fires, 40 hostile impacts, 40 DATA cuts, 40 voltage failures, 40 scanner topology changes; extra composite wave multiple categories concurrently and restore stages. Use independent entities so later death wave works after earlier critical. For events with native game mechanics not instantaneous (FTL travel, projectile impact, door opening), synchronize START on same tick, and separately measure observed completion latency; do not mislabel completion as same tick. Include 1/10/20/40 ship scaling tiers and varied real ship classes (at least 8 distinct hulls if compatible), with canonical 40-briar control baseline for meaningful A/B. Preserve tick-indexed seeds; avoid random global game RNG dependence without snapshot/validation.
+
+Default final ~30 simulated min measured per A/B/B/A + 3min warmup (can auto lengthen when all phase/event coverage would not fit), static baseline + optimized B and optionally optimized B-only before/after for causality; symmetric instrumentation and same event schedule. Native effects may diverge because KIAS acts: record each input and actual world outcome, categorize intended vs unintended divergence instead of falsely enforcing identical final worlds. Persist all wave completion/failure rates and queues.
+
+### Acceptance hard gates
+Builds and source/mapping fingerprints fresh, inventory parity and replay binding valid; 27 preset physical fixture tests (not just compile) PASS/explicit NEEDS_FIX; RoomGate + saved Briar scanner orientation + exterior visual acceptance; native PDC/FTL/guns/collision/crew death + DATA link probes PASS; room tests, UI, persistence, owner/access, native complete driver coverage; event dispatch targets match, no silently skipped wave, no unhandled exception, queues eventually drain or explicit FAIL, no machine lost/faulted. Collect p50/p95/p99/p99.9/max tick, >16.67ms count and longest stall, GC alloc/duration, physics body/contacts, KIAS per phase, command latency, PDC interactions, topology rebuild, CPU/memory, physical correctness, world parity, diagnostic captures. Attribution must distinguish total measured tick vs phase instrumentation overhead and profiler samples; no performance PASS if optional instrumentation was missing.
+
+After every phase write durable progress heartbeat. Full report includes per-tier 1/10/20/40, wave charts and top100 worst tick attribution, deviations, errors, exact commit hashes, environment/host and wall/sim times. Status enum = READY/PASS/FAIL/INCOMPLETE/BLOCKED with explicit requirements evidence; **no 'all tested' if even one driver absent**. A/B/C/D physics may happen before handoff; final full ABBA must WAIT for USER.
